  "worked_solution": "First, we re-write the product using the cube:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[3]{7}\\cdot \\sqrt[3]{7}\\cdot \\sqrt[3]{7}={(\\sqrt[3]{7})}^{3}.\n$$\n\nNow, we use that  the cube and the cube root cancel each other out. So, we have\n\n$$\n{(\\sqrt[3]{7})}^{3}=7.\n$$",
